A||N||8||Fiero5||4 Cyl won't start on it's own||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero5||02-25-2001||03:25 PM||||Hi there fellow Fiero lovers :o)<P>Here is a good one that everyone can put their thinking caps on for...<BR>We are trying to get Fiero1 back on the road. It is an 84SE 4 cyl. She<BR>will start and run great, BUT only if you squirt some gas in the carb<BR>first before turning the key. She won't start on her own. We have been<BR>swapping parts from Fiero10 which is an 84 base model 4cyl., to see what<BR>parts work and what do not.<BR>My father says that the fuses in Fiero1 are fine, the relay works fine and<BR>obviously the fual pump works fine as the engine will run great once you<BR>squirt some gas in the carb first to get it going. <BR>When you turn the key, you do not hear the fuel pump whir on. My dad is<BR>assuming that maybe a wire somewhere is bad, as it doesn't seem to be<BR>getting power to feed the carb gas for startup.<BR>Again, once we get it running via squirting gas in the carb first, it will<BR>run fine all day long, until you turn it back off again :o(<P>Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>Steve & Russ Kelley||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||03:34 PM||||Same thing happened on Jaime's Fiero. I couldn't figure it out. It ended up being the fusible link that connects to the Pos+ Batt cable. It looked fine but was corroded on the inside. I cut it out and replaced it with an inline fuse and it started right up.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Fiero5||02-25-2001||03:50 PM||||My Dad says that it doesn't have any fusible links that he can see. He says that it doesn't have a junction box. He wants to know if anyone knows if it might have some kind of fusible link or similar down on the starter?, as the pos+ lead goes directly to the starter.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                                                                                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/rutland99winner.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||04:10 PM||||I can take a picture tomorrow of the exact location of the fusible link. It was in the wire harness that ran close to the belt. I think the wires run over to the alt. and around the front of the engine. The fusible link was up near the Batt. end of those wires.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||gabriel||02-25-2001||05:03 PM||||I'm just guessing, but I'll betcha everyone you pass on the road knows thats a Fiero!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero5||02-25-2001||05:28 PM||||Actually, believe it or not I still have people quite often ask me when I am in Fiero1 what kind of car it is  LOL<P>Marian had a guy at a busy gas station once that was confused when she popped the trunk rear deck lid for him, so he could put a quart of oil in her Fiero2. He wanted to know why she popped the trunk if she wanted him to add the oil? Then after she told him that was where the engine was, he couldn't figure out where the oil went.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                                                                                                       <IMG SRC="http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/files/dads87GT.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||02-25-2001||06:43 PM||||My 84 Coupe did that and I spent a day trying to track it down before giving up and taking it to my mechanic.  He said it was a fusible link.  $70 later I was back on the road.||||reg||3
Z||000007||Fiero5||02-26-2001||09:59 PM||||Well, I have to say that Fiero64 - good ole' Josh was right on the money!!!<BR>My Dad took another look, and way down under where you could hardly see was a wire hanging. He spliced in a new wire and re-wired it back to the Pos+ and away she went! Fired right up!! Wahoooo!<P>Thanks Josh - You da man!<P>Now if we can just get it down off the bank and out of all the snow! Whew, we are exhausted from shoveling! Those things have a low underbelly  :o)||||reg||6
Z||000008||TheFiero64||02-27-2001||10:10 AM||||I'm glad I could help. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You gona be at the Kick Hill meeting the 10th? I hope to see you and the rest of the family there.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
